12	 *
13	 * Mounted ONCE at the portal shell level (components/portal/Shell.tsx), exactly
14	 * like the terminal dock and the mail composer. Because the App Router keeps
15	 * Shell mounted across in-portal navigation, the whole Matrix subtree — every
16	 * open console, its per-console transcript/input state, and any live server
17	 * terminal websocket inside it — survives moving between dashboard pages. Leave
18	 * Matrix mid-build, wander the portal, come back, and it is exactly as you left
19	 * it (the sidebar "running"/"update" tag tells you when to come back).
20	 *
21	 * How it stays alive:
22	 *   - The workspace is rendered into a fixed panel that occupies the main
23	 *     content region ONLY while the route is /dashboard/build; on every other
24	 *     route the panel is `display:none` but STILL MOUNTED, so React never
25	 *     unmounts BuildStudio/BuildConsole and their sockets keep running.
26	 *   - It is lazy: nothing is fetched or mounted until the customer first opens
27	 *     Matrix (`activated` latches true), so users who never touch it pay nothing.
28	 *   - Data (servers, recent builds, key status) is re-fetched each time the
29	 *     route is entered and passed as fresh props. BuildStudio's console state
30	 *     lives in its own `useState` (initialised once), so refreshed props update
31	 *     the dropdowns/board without ever resetting the open consoles.
32	 *
33	 * The /dashboard/build PAGE is a thin placeholder — this panel covers it.
34	 */
